<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Saïo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1941</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-campaign-world-war-ii">East African campaign (World War II)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Saïo was fought in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in June and July 1941, during the East African campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Troops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/force-publique">Force Publique</a> of the Belgian Congo, under General Auguste-Éduard Gilliaert, attacked the Italian positions, and on 6 July 1941 General Pietro Gazzera surrendered with several thousand men. It was the main Belgian victory of the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-saio.jpg" alt="Battle of Saïo" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belgian_forces_with_captured_Italian_artillery.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
